`@group-members` no longer wakes one object per row. Rendering a row filled `profile_url` by userid, which searches the catalog a second time and then activates the Profile to ask for its URL, so drawing a page of a group cost one activation per person on it — on the endpoint whose whole premise is that a group of a thousand is one query rather than a thousand object loads. A brain already knows its URL. The endpoint has also joined the activation-counting suite that covered the PAS plugins and never covered it, which is where the regression landed unseen. @ericof
